// Rule: Suspicious PowerShell Activity (Event 4104)
// Severity: Medium | MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.001 Command and Scripting Interpreter: PowerShell (Execution)
// Schedule: run every 5 minutes, look back 20 minutes
//   (the lookback was raised from 5 to 20 min because Event-table ingestion lagged behind a 5-minute window)
// Entities: Host -> HostName = Computer
// Known issue: because the rule runs every 5 minutes but looks back 20, each event is matched by
// several runs, which created duplicate incidents. Next fix: add `| where ingestion_time() > ago(5m)`
// so each event only alerts once.
// Data source: dcr-powershell-logs, XPath Microsoft-Windows-PowerShell/Operational!*
// Requires PowerShell Script Block Logging on the host
Event
| where EventID == 4104
| where RenderedDescription has_any ("IEX", "DownloadString", "Net.WebClient", "FromBase64String",
                                     "EncodedCommand", "Invoke-Expression", "DownloadFile")
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, RenderedDescription
